Weather considerations for outdoor rentals usually mean tents, portable air conditioning and drainage, a trade Malaga Event Gear does not work in. What we can answer honestly is the question those guides skip: what does changing weather actually do to the sound, lighting and microphones we do rent, and how does our service actually respond to it. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview. For power, curfews and wind placement specifically for an outdoor wedding, see our [outdoor wedding rental considerations](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) guide.

## Brief Overview

---

The honest, AV specific answer to weather considerations for outdoor rentals is not a tent or a climate control unit, MEG does not supply either. It is who is on site to react when weather shifts during the event. The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) include a live technician who can reposition equipment, add moisture protection to cables, or adjust for wind as conditions change. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) and [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) are self run: our crew delivers, installs and tests the system, then leaves, so nobody is there to react if the weather turns after that.

## Key Highlights

---

- A live technician, included on the Wedding Pack and MICE Pack, can reposition equipment, add cable and moisture protection, or adjust for wind as conditions change during the event. The Eco Pack and Basic MICE Pack run self operated after our crew leaves, with nobody on site to react.
- Wireless microphone receivers, cabling and active electronics all carry real moisture and heat sensitivity. We do not publish a weatherproof rating for any of it.
- Every booking, and every change to one, needs at least 24 hours' notice. The earlier you check the forecast against that window, the more flexibility you actually have.
- We operate delivery only, there is no self pickup option, so our own crew handles transport and retrieval in any weather, not the client.
- We do not stock tents, canopies, generators or portable climate control. Venue provided shelter and power need to be confirmed by the client directly with the venue.

## The Real Difference: A Technician On Site vs a Self Run Setup

Weather risk to AV equipment is not really a product question, MEG does not sell a weatherproof speaker line that costs more, it is a staffing question. On the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), a live technician stays on site throughout the event. If a gust of wind starts pushing a speaker stand, if a light drizzle reaches a cable run, or if a receiver starts dropping signal in the heat, the technician can move the gear, add protection, or adjust the setup in real time.

The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) and the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) do not include that. Our crew delivers, installs and tests the system professionally, then it runs unattended for the rest of the event. That is a fine setup for a sheltered patio or a stable forecast, but it means nobody adjusts the equipment if weather changes after our crew leaves. If your outdoor event has any real chance of shifting weather, that staffing difference matters more than anything printed on a spec sheet.

<InlineCTA />

## What Weather Actually Risks in AV Equipment

Rain, humidity and heat do not affect every piece of gear the same way, and we would rather explain the real risk than claim a blanket weatherproof rating we cannot back up.

- **Wireless microphones and receivers.** Moisture affects wireless RF performance and can cause dropouts or signal degradation. Our technician, when one is on site, can dry, reposition or swap a unit if this starts happening.
- **Cabling and electrical safety.** Wet ground and wet connectors are an electrical safety issue, not just a performance one. Cable runs and connection points need to stay clear of standing water and direct rain exposure.
- **Active PA systems and LED lighting.** Heat affects the electronics inside active speakers and LED fixtures over a long outdoor run, and direct rain exposure is a risk for any of it. None of our equipment carries a published weatherproof certification.

Wind is a related factor for equipment placement specifically, speaker and lighting stand positioning on grass, sand or a windy terrace, which our [outdoor wedding rental considerations](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) guide covers in more depth for wedding venues.

## Forecast Timing and Our 24 Hour Notice Window

All event gear rentals and technical services with MEG must be contracted, or reconfirmed, with a minimum of 24 hours' advance notice, to guarantee scheduling and logistical availability. That is the one hard constraint on reacting to a shifting forecast. If a forecast changes a week out, there is real room to adjust your package, add ons or technician hours before the date. If it changes inside that 24 hour window, any change is still checked against what is actually available that day, not guaranteed. The earlier you check the forecast relative to your event date, the more genuine flexibility you have. Our [managing last minute wedding rental changes](/blog/managing-last-minute-wedding-rental-changes/) guide covers the full mechanics of a late change, including a weather driven indoor to outdoor swap.

## Delivery Only Means Our Crew Handles the Weather, Not You

We operate a delivery only model. There is no self pickup option. That means our own crew transports, installs and retrieves the equipment in whatever weather is happening on the day, rather than leaving a client to load and unload gear in the rain themselves. It is not a weather guarantee for the event itself, but it does mean the physical handling of the equipment, arrival and pickup, stays with people trained to do it, not with a couple or a venue's own staff.

## What MEG Does Not Supply

To be direct about scope: we do not stock tents, canopies, marquees, generators, portable air conditioning, heaters or any drainage solution. If your outdoor venue needs shelter from rain or sun, or backup power beyond what the venue itself provides, that has to be arranged separately and confirmed with your venue, not assumed as part of an MEG package. Tell us what shelter and power your venue already has when you book, so our technician can plan the AV setup around it rather than around equipment we do not bring.

