Our services focus on Malaga and extend to Granada for rentals over 400 euros. There is no fixed booking window, only availability, so reach out once your date and venue are confirmed, and tell us about your venue's shelter and power situation at that point. See our [booking timeline](/blog/timeline-for-booking-wedding-rentals/) guide for more on that.

## Conclusion

Weather considerations for outdoor rentals, for the equipment MEG actually supplies, come down to who is watching the gear, not a weatherproof rating we do not publish. A live technician on the Wedding Pack and MICE Pack can react to changing weather during the event, a self run Eco Pack or Basic MICE Pack setup cannot. Check the forecast early against our 24 hour notice window, confirm your venue's own shelter and power with them directly, and our crew handles the rest, delivery, setup and pickup, in whatever weather the day brings. [Contact us](/contact/) to check availability for your date.

## FAQs

### Does a technician stay on site to react if the weather changes during my event?

Only on the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), which include a live technician throughout the event who can reposition equipment, add moisture protection to cables, or adjust for wind as conditions change. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) and [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) are self run after our crew installs and tests the system, so nobody is there to react afterward.

### Is your AV equipment weatherproof?

We do not publish a weatherproof rating for any of our equipment. Wireless microphone receivers are moisture sensitive and can drop signal, cabling and connectors are an electrical safety risk in wet conditions, and heat affects the electronics in active PA systems and LED lighting over a long outdoor run. A live technician, where one is included, is what actually manages that risk in real time.

### Do you supply tents, canopies or generators for outdoor weather protection?

No. We do not stock tents, canopies, marquees, generators, portable air conditioning or heaters. Venue provided shelter and power need to be confirmed by you directly with your venue. Tell us what is available when you book so our technician can plan the AV setup around it.

### If the forecast changes close to my event date, how much flexibility do I have?

All bookings and changes to one need at least 24 hours' notice to guarantee scheduling and logistical availability. Checking the forecast a week out leaves real room to adjust your package or add ons. Checking it inside that 24 hour window still gets an availability check, not a guarantee. See our [managing last minute wedding rental changes](/blog/managing-last-minute-wedding-rental-changes/) guide for the full mechanics.

### Who handles the equipment if it rains, me or your crew?

Our crew. We operate delivery only, there is no self pickup option, so our own trained team transports, installs and retrieves every system regardless of weather, rather than a client handling the gear themselves.

### How does wind affect where you place speakers and lighting outdoors?

Wind changes where a speaker stand or lighting rig can safely stand on grass, sand or a windy terrace. Our technician reads the actual ground and wind exposure on site. Our [outdoor wedding rental considerations](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) guide covers this in more depth for wedding venues specifically.
